1
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:35,050
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:37,690
[Episode 26]

3
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,000
Do you think I'm

4
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,229
too full of myself

5
00:01:44,759 --> 00:01:45,690
and too useless?

6
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,070
I can't even protect my own brand

7
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:48,930
and employees.

8
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,310
What kind of boss am I?

9
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:54,039
Why am I even running a company?

10
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:58,310
Shut it down then.

11
00:02:01,310 --> 00:02:03,110
You should believe in yourself.

12
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:05,730
You have courage, your own ideas,

13
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:07,470
and a sharp sense

14
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:08,840
of the clothing market.

15
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,190
All these mean that

16
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,210
you can definitely become

17
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:13,920
a qualified, good boss.

18
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:17,430
Starting a business

19
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:20,400
always has its ups and downs.

20
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:21,960
But don't worry.

21
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:25,000
No matter how big the storm

22
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,060
our company faces,

23
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:29,910
I will surely be there with you

24
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:30,770
to the very end.

25
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:45,810
Are you moved? Don't cry.

26
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:47,630
No, I'm not.

27
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:55,310
What do you mean by being there
with me to the very end?

28
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:57,310
You're a partner.
That's what you should do.

29
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:58,079
Yeah, yeah.

30
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,030
We're now

31
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:01,430
in the same boat.

32
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,130
Therefore,

33
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,710
I have to give it my all

34
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,050
and share weal and woe with you.

35
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,230
But I'm tired.

36
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,690
I want to take a rest.

37
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:27,750
I'll leave the company to you for now.

38
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:29,410
Once you clear the inventory,

39
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:31,410
you can take all the money left.

40
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:37,680
Okay.

41
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,329
It's good to take a rest.

42
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:48,070
Let's go. I'll escort you home.

43
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:45,960
♪ But your shoulders allow me
to drop my disguise ♪

44
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:51,470
♪ If there's nothing left tomorrow ♪

45
00:04:53,159 --> 00:05:01,430
♪ I still want to watch the sunset
with you ♪

46
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:54,550
This one.

47
00:04:55,510 --> 00:04:56,800
And this one.

48
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:58,430
And then

49
00:04:58,830 --> 00:04:59,720
submit.

50
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,040
See?

51
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:04,370
Online shopping isn't that hard, huh?

52
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,830
It used to be so hard

53
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,160
to get you to buy some clothes

54
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,510
with your own money.

55
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,120
Now that you know our daughter's

56
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:14,520
business is struggling,

57
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,390
you bought

58
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,950
several sets at once.

59
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:19,190
You've got clothes

60
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:20,220
for all 4 seasons.

61
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,540
I'm killing two birds with one stone,

62
00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:26,200
helping both our daughter and son.

63
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:28,390
Well,

64
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:29,630
they are running

65
00:05:29,630 --> 00:05:31,220
this online store together,

66
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:31,950
aren't they?

67
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:34,950
It's not easy for young people
to start a business.

68
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:36,070
We can't let them lose

69
00:05:36,070 --> 00:05:37,310
every penny they've put into it

70
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:38,909
because of that stupid mess.

71
00:05:40,270 --> 00:05:41,730
A mother's selfless love.

72
00:05:41,950 --> 00:05:42,950
Even I am touched.

73
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:44,070
Enough.

74
00:05:45,270 --> 00:05:46,020
Qi Shi said

75
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:47,680
she'd be back for dinner later.

76
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,620
I bought a fish for her.

77
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:49,680
Go clean it.

78
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,690
I'll cook it for her.

79
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:54,630
See?

80
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:56,430
It's too late.

81
00:05:56,430 --> 00:05:57,720
She's already back.

82
00:05:58,190 --> 00:05:58,920
Coming.

83
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:00,680
Coming.

84
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:02,770
Sweetie,

85
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,600
welcome back.

86
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:04,750
Welcome back.

87
00:06:04,750 --> 00:06:06,150
-Dad.
-You must be tired.

88
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,290
Go get some rest.

89
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,200
I'll cook fish for you later.

90
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,170
Are you thirsty?

91
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:13,230
Would you like me
to wash some fruit for you?

92
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:15,810
I'm hungry and thirsty right now.

93
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,840
I just want to be spoon-fed.

94
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,190
Okay, just a moment.

95
00:06:19,190 --> 00:06:20,250
I will go wash them.

96
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,750
Being spoon-fed is no problem,

97
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,430
but you have to pour your own water.

98
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:24,510
You rarely come back home,

99
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:26,040
so you have to do something.

100
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,260
I'm going to cook fish for you.

101
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:42,950
Si.

102
00:06:43,830 --> 00:06:44,430
Come here.

103
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:48,159
I have something to tell everyone.

104
00:06:48,159 --> 00:06:49,790
Our company's not doing well

105
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,659
currently.

106
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:53,190
Judging from the financial data,

107
00:06:53,190 --> 00:06:54,920
we can't make up for the losses

108
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:55,950
anytime soon

109
00:06:56,830 --> 00:06:58,360
through normal marketing.

110
00:06:58,720 --> 00:06:59,360
The priority now

111
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,500
is to deal with all this inventory

112
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,230
and customer returns.

113
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,380
I've thought about it.

114
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,160
We need to categorize the products.

115
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,120
For the ones that sell well,

116
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:09,180
we can offer appropriate discounts.

117
00:07:09,830 --> 00:07:11,120
For the harder-to-sell ones,

118
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,480
we can bundle them at a low price
to sell through other channels.

119
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,920
This way, we can clear the inventory

120
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,140
and recover funds quickly

121
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:16,920
to ease the financial pressure

122
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,780
on our company.

123
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:19,720
What do you think?

124
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,120
This is a solution plan

125
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,180
I've put together.

126
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:23,850
Take a look.

127
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,400
Almost there.

128
00:07:56,190 --> 00:07:57,630
Excuse me, may I ask

129
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,740
where you bought your jacket?

130
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:01,810
I just got it from an online store.

131
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:04,360
Did you buy other pieces

132
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,510
from that store?

133
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:06,720
Nope.

134
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,360
Could you tell me

135
00:08:10,870 --> 00:08:12,390
why you bought it?

136
00:08:12,470 --> 00:08:13,310
Did you like how it looked,

137
00:08:13,310 --> 00:08:15,040
or was there some other reason?

138
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:16,890
Why so many questions?

139
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:24,480
You, too?

140
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,240
Why did you want

141
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,289
to play ring toss

142
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:33,530
with our eyesight?

143
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,360
It was exactly because of my bad eyesight.

144
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,150
When I was little

145
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,390
and walked past these stalls with my mom,

146
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:39,600
she never let me play.

147
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:42,120
The more she said no,
the more I wanted to play.

148
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,850
How would I know if I didn't try?

149
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,550
What if I was like a genius girl

150
00:08:45,550 --> 00:08:46,410
in a comic book,

151
00:08:46,550 --> 00:08:47,000
with the power

152
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
to break through innate obstacles?

153
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,400
But it turns out...

154
00:08:53,790 --> 00:08:54,720
It turns out

155
00:08:56,290 --> 00:08:58,150
that we're just ordinary people.

156
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,000
You're not ordinary at all.

157
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:03,250
My mom said that for albinos,

158
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,480
just maintaining

159
00:09:04,510 --> 00:09:06,380
a normal daily life is good enough.

160
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:07,440
Don't even think about doing

161
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,100
anything earth-shattering.

162
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,330
But you actually opened a shop.

163
00:09:11,450 --> 00:09:12,760
How is opening a shop

164
00:09:12,790 --> 00:09:14,240
earth-shattering?

165
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:16,520
Now I feel like

166
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:19,390
I-I just don't know how to run a shop.

167
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,600
I only had passion,

168
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:23,030
rushed forward blindly,

169
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:23,740
and ended up

170
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,100
betraying everyone's trust.

171
00:09:26,250 --> 00:09:27,360
But the fact that you asked me

172
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,490
all those questions

173
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:29,790
means

174
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,240
you haven't given up on this shop

175
00:09:32,430 --> 00:09:34,360
and still want to do better, right?

176
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:35,850
Let me think.

177
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:38,720
When I bought this jacket,

178
00:09:39,030 --> 00:09:40,890
I just searched a random keyword,

179
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,390
and the site recommended

180
00:09:42,390 --> 00:09:43,720
a bunch of similar ones.

181
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,520
Then why did you choose this one?

182
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,390
Because...

183
00:09:48,670 --> 00:09:49,400
it was cheap.

184
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,080
So

185
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:56,150
there's nothing special

186
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,790
about its design,

187
00:09:57,790 --> 00:09:58,240
huh?

188
00:09:58,310 --> 00:09:59,120
It's merely

189
00:09:59,150 --> 00:10:00,280
an ordinary jacket,

190
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:02,120
not even as special as we are.

191
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,140
Look at our skin

192
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:04,240
and hair.

193
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:06,570
We just stand out in any crowd.

194
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:17,270
Order 5748153357, right?

195
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:19,610
I see it.

196
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:22,390
I see you put the reason

197
00:10:22,390 --> 00:10:23,210
for return

198
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,970
as a defective product, right?

199
00:10:38,270 --> 00:10:40,270
A big sale for women's fashion!

200
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:41,750
Come on! Take a look!

201
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,870
Come on, beautiful. Come and take a look.

202
00:10:43,870 --> 00:10:44,870
Women's fashion.

203
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:16,640
[Prime Era]

204
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,960
Have you forgotten when you were little?

205
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:30,870
You kept your wrist still

206
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:32,600
and ended up getting beaten up.

207
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,200
You've been staying at home

208
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,400
for a week now, right?

209
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:43,560
What's going on with your company?

210
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,970
No idea. Cao Xin is managing it.

211
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:47,570
You can't

212
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,120
just leave it all to him

213
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:51,120
and rest at home every day.

214
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:53,440
What?

215
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:56,570
Are you caring about your biological son?

216
00:11:58,440 --> 00:11:59,670
My biological son doesn't

217
00:11:59,670 --> 00:12:01,790
eat and live on my dime every day,

218
00:12:03,030 --> 00:12:04,430
without doing anything.

219
00:12:05,070 --> 00:12:06,550
Do I owe you this from a past life?

220
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:07,000
Huh?

221
00:12:08,550 --> 00:12:09,960
Mom, don't deny it.

222
00:12:10,790 --> 00:12:12,520
I was just wondering back then.

223
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:15,820
You were really biased towards Cao Xin.

224
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:16,840
He ate

225
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:18,050
all the buns

226
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,350
we only made once

227
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,670
every half a month.

228
00:12:23,750 --> 00:12:25,520
Girl, you're so petty.

229
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:26,750
That was ages ago,

230
00:12:26,770 --> 00:12:28,100
and you still remember?

231
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:28,870
Then how about

232
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:30,670
all those meals I cooked for you?

233
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,790
How many sweaters did I knit for you?

234
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:34,450
How much did I worry about you?

235
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:38,390
Don't knit little flowers for me anymore.

236
00:12:38,390 --> 00:12:39,600
I'm a grown-up now.

237
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:42,720
And knitting little flowers
is quite a hassle.

238
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,580
How pretty this little flower is.

239
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,120
It's just so pretty.

240
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:50,750
I think...

241
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,600
it was when you were in primary school.

242
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:56,330
You started to care about your looks.

243
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:57,440
You thought the sweaters I knitted for you

244
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,120
were ugly.

245
00:12:58,920 --> 00:12:59,960
Then I...

246
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:01,490
I tried to figure out a way.

247
00:13:01,810 --> 00:13:02,440
I figured it out

248
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,360
by knitting a little flower like this

249
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,600
on the cuff

250
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:08,150
or the chest for you,

251
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,870
so you could look a bit prettier

252
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:11,800
and a bit special

253
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,170
when you wear it.

254
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,770
♪ When the world falls still ♪

255
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:18,440
Actually...

256
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:19,790
♪ There is nothing left to argue ♪

257
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,080
In my eyes,

258
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:22,560
♪ I stand at the crossroads ♪

259
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,580
whether you're white-haired

260
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:25,470
♪ While memories flood the station ♪

261
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:24,390
or blue-eyed,

262
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:26,960
you are one of a kind.

263
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:31,320
My daughter is the best.

264
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,910
♪ Who doesn't want to be born ♪

265
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:33,410
♪ In a world of love? ♪

266
00:13:33,950 --> 00:13:37,160
♪ But how do you keep enduring ♪

267
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:36,870
Mom.

268
00:13:37,180 --> 00:13:40,640
♪ When every hope has come apart ♪

269
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,200
Thank you.

270
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:40,390
Thank me for what?

271
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,440
Time for lunch.

272
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,870
Come on, lend me the sweater.

273
00:13:43,870 --> 00:13:44,480
Lend it to me.

274
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,320
W-What for?

275
00:13:45,550 --> 00:13:46,390
I'm not eating, Dad.

276
00:13:46,390 --> 00:13:48,080
I'll come back and eat another day.

277
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,750
I haven't finished knitting yet!

278
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:50,810
You're not eating?

279
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,600
I figured out a way.

280
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,960
The core of originality is innovation,

281
00:13:56,390 --> 00:13:58,230
♪ Moonlight casts a glow
on the windowsill ♪

282
00:13:58,450 --> 00:14:00,980
♪ While shadows linger close by ♪

283
00:13:58,580 --> 00:13:59,570
a one-of-a-kind

284
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,460
brand concept.

285
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:02,270
I kept talking about

286
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,250
♪ I've slowly learned to confess ♪

287
00:14:02,270 --> 00:14:03,470
originality before,

288
00:14:03,790 --> 00:14:04,840
but all I did was

289
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:07,450
♪ My loneliness to myself ♪

290
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,600
produce the clothes designed

291
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:07,390
by Yuanyuan.

292
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:09,600
But I never thought about

293
